{
  "type": "flashcard",
  "id": "ch2-4-flashcards",
  "title": "Complex Numbers",
  "cards": [
    {
      "front": "What is the [[kw:imaginary unit i]]?",
      "back": [
        "i = √–1, so i² = –1.",
        "It is not a real number; it's used to build complex numbers."
      ]
    },
    {
      "front": "Define a [[kw:complex number]] in standard form.",
      "back": [
        "a + bi, where a and b are real numbers.",
        "a is the [[imp:real part]], bi is the [[imp:imaginary part]].",
        "Every real number is a complex number with b=0."
      ]
    },
    {
      "front": "Write √–25 in standard form.",
      "back": [
        "√–25 = √25 · i = 5i.",
        "Standard form: 0 + 5i (or just 5i)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "front": "Add (3+2i) + (4 – 5i).",
      "back": [
        "Add real parts: 3+4=7.",
        "Add imaginary parts: 2i + (–5i) = –3i.",
        "Result: 7 – 3i."
      ]
    },
    {
      "front": "Subtract (5 – 2i) – (3 + 4i).",
      "back": [
        "Distribute the minus: 5 – 2i – 3 – 4i.",
        "Combine real: 5 – 3 = 2.",
        "Combine imaginary: –2i – 4i = –6i. Result: 2 – 6i."
      ]
    },
    {
      "front": "What is the additive inverse of 2 – 3i?",
      "back": [
        "–(2 – 3i) = –2 + 3i.",
        "Their sum is (2 – 3i) + (–2 + 3i) = 0."
      ]
    },
    {
      "front": "Multiply (4)( –2 + 3i).",
      "back": [
        "Distribute: 4(–2) + 4(3i) = –8 + 12i.",
        "Standard form: –8 + 12i."
      ]
    },
    {
      "front": "Multiply (2 – i)(4 + 3i) using FOIL.",
      "back": [
        "FOIL: 8 + 6i – 4i – 3i².",
        "Combine: 8 + 2i – 3(–1) = 8 + 2i + 3 = 11 + 2i.",
        "Remember i² = –1."
      ]
    },
    {
      "front": "What is the [[kw:complex conjugate]] of a + bi?",
      "back": [
        "a – bi.",
        "Product (a+bi)(a–bi) = a² + b² (real)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "front": "Find the conjugate of 4 – 7i and multiply them.",
      "back": [
        "Conjugate: 4 + 7i.",
        "Product: (4 – 7i)(4 + 7i) = 16 – 49i² = 16 + 49 = 65.",
        "65 is real."
      ]
    },
    {
      "front": "Divide (2 + 3i) / (4 – 2i) and write in standard form.",
      "back": [
        "Multiply numerator and denominator by conjugate 4+2i.",
        "Numerator: (2+3i)(4+2i)=8+4i+12i+6i²=8+16i–6=2+16i.",
        "Denominator: 16 – 4i²=16+4=20.",
        "Result: 2/20 + (16/20)i = 1/10 + 4/5 i."
      ]
    },
    {
      "front": "Simplify 1 / i.",
      "back": [
        "Multiply top and bottom by i: i / i² = i / (–1) = –i.",
        "Standard form: 0 – i."
      ]
    },
    {
      "front": "When do quadratic equations have [[kw:complex solutions]]?",
      "back": [
        "When the discriminant b² – 4ac is negative.",
        "Solutions are of the form p ± qi, a conjugate pair."
      ]
    },
    {
      "front": "Solve x² + 9 = 0.",
      "back": [
        "x² = –9 → x = ±√–9 = ±3i.",
        "Solutions: 3i and –3i."
      ]
    },
    {
      "front": "Solve 2x² – 3x + 5 = 0 using the quadratic formula.",
      "back": [
        "a=2, b=–3, c=5. Discriminant = 9 – 40 = –31.",
        "x = [3 ± √(–31)] / 4 = [3 ± i√31] / 4.",
        "(3/4) ± (√31/4) i."
      ]
    }
  ],
